      {
        "id": 255780,
        "name": "OddballPaladin",
        "username": "OddballPaladin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/d26b3c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2023-12-09T18:10:14.648Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\" data-post=\"25\" data-topic=\"30367\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The bit about Legacy’s reaction to the team-up is excellent, and Senator Parsons’ response is even better.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>“I should go. They could be in trouble!”<br>\n“Dear, is the news talking about a running gunfight, or massive numbers of bodies?”<br>\n“Well… no, but-”<br>\n“They’re fine, dear.”</p>\n<p>Okay, now I want to know what kind of interactions Amanda and Senator Parsons have had. I like the stories about the discovery and kindling of personhood. I briefly got into DC stuff with No Man’s Land because of the character of Cassandra Cain (so you can imagine how quickly I left again). Issac in the first two season of The Orville (I haven’t been able to watch S3 yet) and his romance arc was interesting, or some of the stuff for Data in Star Trek (not the emotion chip, but definitely the dreams episodes), and the like. There was a bit of this with the questions in the past about Setback trying to take her on a date, but I feel like Pete is the wrong person for that kind of story.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2023-12-09T18:10:14.648Z",
